# smalltalk-professional-v1: The formal register: a formal variant of every situation that has one, one priority above its base situation, so that with this collection loaded the formal phrasing wins. Load at most one register collection that overrides (this one).
# Generated by tools/smalltalk/build.mjs from tools/smalltalk/taxonomy.json and the accepted records of jobs/smalltalk-replies; do not edit by hand.

# The formal register: while the conversation's register is formal, whenever a situation applies its formal variant applies too, one priority higher, so it wins its part.
@stf_r_formal rule
  when cv_register formal
  when cv_applies ?s
  when st_formal_variant ?s ?v
  then cv_applies ?v

# Two variants tie as their bases do: the variant of the base that outranks the other outranks it too.
@stf_r_formal_ties rule
  when st_formal_variant ?a ?v
  when st_formal_variant ?b ?w
  when cv_situation_outranks ?a ?b
  then cv_situation_outranks ?v ?w

